<p>Use the following procedure to arrange eight pages on one sheet using 
 a layout suitable for pamphlets. Cut and fold the sheet according to the 
 lines to make a pamphlet.</p>
<p>If the orientation of the first page is portrait, the pamphlet will 
 open to the left. If it is landscape, it will open to the top.</p>
<p><img alt="" class="help-img" height="242" loading="lazy" src="~/images/help/ori03.gif" width="280"/></p>
<p>Red line: Cut line / Dotted line: Mountain fold / Solid line: Valley 
 fold</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Imposition</span> menu 
 on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">On</span> in the 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Pamphlet:</span> list.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Draw Border</span> 
 check box to print lines on the sheet for cutting and folding, if necessary.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
